diagnosis:
Producers do not export what consumers need. The boundary 'no record type standing in for an object' (`cluster/cdk8s/AGENTS.md:8-13`) left a bare string constant as the only sanctioned carrier for a fact that crosses modules. Results:
- one port is written 6 times in one module (`ntfy.py:78` defines it; 221, 252, 256, 269-270 and 287 reuse it);
- `<cluster>-app` and `<name>-rw.<ns>.svc` are derived by hand 12 times (`terraform.py:33`, `atuin/user_provisioner.py:38-39`);
- the `external-creds-reader` literal appears 19 times;
- a consumer re-declares a producer's bearer name (`agentplane/staging.py:84-87` against `ha_mcp.py:84-85`);
- `single_secret_store` returns a `str` (`external_secrets/single_secret_store.py:22-30`).
Only `Service(selector=deployment)` and Settings-derived env names hold by construction.

Cross-cutting pod policy was written against one dialect. `apply_pod_spec_patches` and `attract_to_zone` take a cdk8s-plus `Workload` (`pod_spec_patches.py:22-23`, `node_scheduling.py:13-14`), but 54 workloads are raw `k8s.Kube*`, and `SandboxTemplate` and `ScaledJob` embed their own pod types. Hardening is carried four ways:
- constructor keywords;
- `WRITABLE_ROOT` (`container_security.py:10-14`);
- the fluent-only patch;
- literal structs (`nix_cache/attic.py:272-285`, `agent_workspaces.py:102-124`).
Placement literals are spread wider still: 14 modules keep a local zone constant, `"hil-ovh"` appears 35 times, Helm values carry 25 `nodeSelector` dicts in 17 modules, and the control-plane taint key is spelled in 33 modules.

Enforcement depends on the author remembering. Fleet rules are registered per chart by an explicit `add_fleet_rules` call (`fleet_rules.py:147-148`) on 12 of 188 charts, and `pod_hardening` does not walk `ScaledJob` (`fleet_rules.py:25-33`). Node facts are restated at each node:
- `SOPS_DECRYPTION` is passed by hand at 51 nodes, against `sops_decryption` at 6;
- 42 health-check entries are typed out (for example `dns_automation.py:84-91`), against `flux.health_checks` at 5 call sites;
- 21 of 39 stateful Kustomizations lack the Orphan that `cluster/cdk8s/AGENTS.md:16-20` requires.
The graph check has the same gap: `OPERATOR_CRDS` (`cluster/validation/crd_layering.py`) misses 16 rendered custom-resource kinds, and `parse_cluster` reads only `kustomizations.k8s.yaml`, so haku-state-workloads and the gaffer-private bridge are not graph nodes at all (#7763).

Authorization is kept in sync by hand. Copying one Secret between namespaces has at least five mechanisms:
- the external-creds roster;
- `single_secret_store` per-pair stores built from the consumer's chart;
- app-owned ESO-ServiceAccount stores (`ntfy.py:92-122`);
- reflector mirrors;
- ClusterExternalSecret.
Store namespace allowlists are hand-kept copies of the consumer list (the outages are recorded in `TODO.md`; `external_secrets/config.py:98-121`). The committed YAML has three sources for the same `flux-system/external-creds-reader` ServiceAccount: two live Kustomizations (generated/dns-automation, k8s/github-secrets-sync-secrets) and the parked `k8s/parked/cloud-agent-tf`.

The dedup PRs treat symptoms, because there was no target to dedupe toward. Each adds another shape for a job that already has one:
- a TypedDict kwargs spread (#8109);
- policy constants (#8108, #8115);
- a composite with 12+ knobs that returns `None` (#8114);
- thin constructor wrappers (#8106, and the merged #8113).
#8111's combinator grew an `include_dns` flag after the owner objected to callers indexing its result.

The Flux graph was built for readiness, so it grew tiny units, edges that gate on runtime state, and `wait` everywhere. On devel 1faf6d5f22 there are 182 Kustomizations and 426 `dependsOn` edges:
- only 155 are admission edges: 137 to a CRD provider, 11 to a `failurePolicy: Fail` webhook, 7 to a `postBuild` source;
- the other 271 wait on runtime state: 34 on the ESO store unit, 25 on `forgejo-images`, 18 on `tofu-state-db`, 18 on `gateway`, 17 on `seaweedfs-cluster`, 27 on namespace units, and the rest on databases, services and ordering;
- `wait` is true on 129 nodes, and 101 of them are unsuspended and gate nothing admission needs;
- 71 of 176 measurable units render 3 objects or fewer, and one postBuild ConfigMap (`cert-manager-issuer-config`) puts reflector upstream of 118 nodes.
The owner is moving the graph to admission-only edges (#7094, and the merged #7441, #7458, #7495, #7541, #7545 and #7559) because the tiny units cost reconcile time and I/O, but the cdk8s layer still defaults `wait=True` (`flux.py:118`, since #7690) and nothing checks that an edge is justified.

one_service:
`ntfy.py` (338 lines) is a typical small HTTP service. It uses:
- construct classes: `Deployment`, `Service`, `ServiceMonitor`, `ExternalSecret`;
- resource functions: `https_route`, `cnpg.cluster`;
- a mutator that writes a JSON patch: `apply_pod_spec_patches`;
- value factories: `http_probe`, `metadata()`, and a module-local `_secret_env`;
- an opt-in validation: `fleet_rules.add_fleet_rules(chart)`;
- a Flux node that also synthesizes its chart and writes its own `kustomization.yaml` (`ntfy.py:307-338`).
The `PORT` constant is threaded by hand into 6 places, `_LABELS` into 5, and the UID `65532` is written 4 times. The route names its backend as the string `NAME`, not the Service it builds.

